-- title:
--   Inertia-fixed elements of widehatℚ̄ᵥ: valuations and n-th roots
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $A$ be a valuation subring of an algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$, and assume $A$ lies over $p$ in the sense that the image of $p$ in the algebraic closure is a non-unit of $A$. Write $\widehat{K}$ for the completion of the algebraic closure with respect to the valuation attached to $A$, equipped with its canonical valuation $\mathrm{v}$ and with the action of the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$; call an element of $\widehat{K}$ inertia-fixed when it is fixed by every element of the decomposition subgroup that lies in the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. The theorem asserts the conjunction of two statements. First, every non-zero inertia-fixed $x \in \widehat{K}$ satisfies $\mathrm{v}(x) = \mathrm{v}(p)^{n}$ for some integer $n$, where $p$ is viewed in $\widehat{K}$ via the natural map from $\mathbb{N}$. Second, for every natural number $n$ not divisible by $p$ and every inertia-fixed $\mu \in \widehat{K}$ with $\mathrm{v}(\mu) = 1$, there exists an inertia-fixed $\rho \in \widehat{K}$ with $\rho^{n} = \mu$.
--
--   These are the two properties of the inertia invariants of the completion of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ at a place above $p$ that are used later: the value group of the invariants is generated by $\mathrm{v}(p)$, and the units of the invariants are $n$-divisible for $n$ prime to $p$ (reflecting the algebraically closed residue field and Hensel's lemma), although only these two consequences, and not the field structure, are asserted. The result is used in the construction of the period field in the Cerednik–Drinfeld/Mumford part of the development.
